# Rocci CLI reference

This page documents the `rocci` binary only. `rocdown` is the
[Rocdown CLI](/docs/rocdown/cli/).

Until a distribution exists, the spelling is
`cargo run -q -p rocci-cli --`. Examples below write `rocci`.

## Run

```sh
rocci run [ENTRY] [serve options]
```

Standalone directory (`rocci run .` or `rocci run <dir>`), standalone
`.rocci` file, or custom directory/`main.roc`. A standalone directory
resolves a unique entry (`[app].entry`, then unique `@init` / `@context`,
then unique `@get:view("/")`, then a single `.rocci`). Two process inits
in one tree fail. Bare `rocci run` still defaults to `main.roc`. Starts
HTTP and opens a preview window by default. Extra args after the entry go
to the Roc binary. Generated apps pin the in-tree Rocci platform
(`crates/rocci-platform`). `--platform rocci` is accepted and is now the
default. `--http-module` is not this platform.

## View

```sh
rocci view INPUT --component NAME [--arg name=val]
```

Preview one component. HTTP declarations are ignored. `--component Hello`
and `--component hello` both work.

## Build

```sh
rocci build INPUT [-o OUTPUT]
```

Lower one `.rocci` file to Roc. `-o` writes a file; otherwise stdout.

## Validate

```sh
rocci validate [rocci.toml]
```

Parse and validate configuration. Unknown fields and unsafe hosts are
errors. Default path `rocci.toml`. Exit non-zero on failure.

## Build release

```sh
rocci build --release INPUT [-o OUTPUT] [--target x64musl|arm64musl]
```

Package a Linux **server** plus `assets/` (not a macOS `.app`). `INPUT`
may be an app directory, a standalone `.rocci`, or `rocci.toml`.
`--target` requires `--release`.

## Browse

```sh
rocci browse [ROOTS…]
```

Component gallery.

## Playground

```sh
rocci playground INPUT [--mode wasm|local]
```

`--mode wasm` (default) runs in a worker and does not snapshot HTML.
`--mode local` can snapshot through native Roc.

The public site hosts the same WASM workbench at `/playground/`. It
lowers source to generated Roc and AST; HTML preview is not available
there.

## Render

```sh
rocci render INPUT [--fragment] [-o OUTPUT]
```

`Html.render` snapshot. `--fragment` skips the document wrapper.

## Inspect

```sh
rocci inspect INPUT [--ast]
```

Components, fixtures, styles, handlers, generated Roc, and source-map
segments. Segments always print; there is no `--segments` flag. `--ast`
adds the S-expression tree.

## Ast

```sh
rocci ast INPUT
```

Parse tree only.

## Test

```sh
rocci test [PATH]
```

Compile each `.rocci` file (or each `.rocci` under a directory; default
`.`) that declares `@test`, stage a type module with an `expect` trailer,
and run `roc test` on that module. Files without tests are skipped (exit
0). Rocci diagnostics or a failing `roc test` exit non-zero.

## Bundle

```sh
rocci bundle [--config rocci.toml] [--target …]
```

Ad-hoc signed macOS `.app`. Host-native; `--target` is rejected for
`.app`. Production signing is planned.

## Datastar

```sh
rocci datastar pin VERSION [--app PATH]
rocci datastar update [--app PATH]
```

Pin or upgrade the Datastar JS asset. `run` does not auto-upgrade.

## Serve options

Shared by `run`, `view`, `browse`, and `playground`:

| Option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--no-window` | off | Serve without the preview window |
| `--no-live-reload` | off | Pause automatic refresh; watch still rebuilds |
| `--log-handlers` | off | Log matched handlers to stderr / Dev Console |
| `-v` / `--verbose` | off | Per-module template timings, listen heartbeats, and Roc `--timings` / `--verbose` from `roc build --opt=dev`. Phase start/done lines always print. |
| `--port PORT\|auto` | `auto` with a window; `8000` with `--no-window` | Also `ROC_BASIC_WEBSERVER_PORT` |

## Experimental: WASI HTTP module

```sh
rocci build --http-module INPUT.rocci [-o http-module.wasm]
```

`INPUT.rocci` is the **entry** (the file with `@init` / routes), not a
directory and not a file list. Discovery matches `rocci run`: every
`.rocci` under the standalone app root plus authored `.roc` helpers.

Writes a WASI 0.3 `wasi:http/service` **component** against the sibling
`../roc-basic-webserver` wasm32 platform (or `ROCCI_BASIC_WEBSERVER`).
**Not** apply `--host wasm`, and **not** a musl `--release` process.
Missing fork or missing `roc` is an error. Serve with
`wasmtime serve -Sp3 -Scli`. Sqlite apps need `--env DB_PATH=…` and
`--dir=host::guest`. `--http-module` writes `<dest>.assets/`; map it with
`--dir=<dest>.assets::/assets`. `rocci run` stays the native Rocci
platform. `--http-module` still requires basic-webserver 0.16.0 / the
sibling fork wasm32 target. Still omitted: Cmd, in-guest TLS, desktop URL.
